From: atvoicu <avoicu@google.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Mar 2018 14:45:14 -0700
Subject: Add missing skip prefix for some SKIPIF messages

PHP 5.6 never got this change (PHP 7.2.5). Only the bug63000 part is
taken: without the prefix the test, which is for macOS only, also runs on
Linux, where it fails on a build machine without network access.

(cherry picked from commit 17ed2f21cfcf25f3c992b359c672171159d3516c)
---
 ext/sockets/tests/bug63000.phpt | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ext/sockets/tests/bug63000.phpt b/ext/sockets/tests/bug63000.phpt
index 6f9ebea..9eef44c 100644
--- a/ext/sockets/tests/bug63000.phpt
+++ b/ext/sockets/tests/bug63000.phpt
@@ -6,7 +6,7 @@ if (!extension_loaded('sockets')) {
     die('skip sockets extension not available.');
 }
 if (PHP_OS !== 'Darwin') {
-    die('is not OSX.');
+    die('skip Is not OSX.');
 }
 $socket = @socket_create(AF_INET, SOCK_DGRAM, SOL_UDP);
 if ($socket === false) {
